Environment setup: development tools, IDEs, version control, build and CI tools.
Coding: writing source code module by module according to the LLD.
Code review: peer review, pair programming, and static analysis to catch defects early.
Unit testing: developers test each module in isolation as they write it.
Integration: combining modules and checking that interfaces work together.
Database and API implementation: creating schemas, endpoints, and connections.
Documentation: code comments, API docs, and developer guides.

